// ui-catalogue.jsonc: the machine-readable catalogue of the user interface: its design tokens, the contrast pairs every theme is held to, and the theme presets (docs/design-system.md, "Layer 1: tokens and themes" and "The catalogue").
// Not a part of spec.jsonc: like deploy.jsonc it is a file of its own that tools read. scripts/ui-tokens.mjs reads it and `npm run generate` writes one stylesheet per preset into web/src/styles/generated; it refuses a preset whose contrast pair falls below its minimum, in either scheme and for every variant. Later sections of the catalogue (fonts, primitives, layouts, patterns and so on) are added to this file.
//
// Shape of the sections written so far:
//   tokens:        every token, its group, its type, and (for durations) the value under reduced motion. The CSS custom property of a token is its id behind two hyphens.
//   contrastPairs: foreground token, the tokens it sits on, and the minimum ratio (4.5 text, 3 non-text, WCAG 1.4.11).
//   No pills (D-DS-31): no token, primitive or pattern is a capsule. scripts/ui-tokens.mjs refuses a token whose id names a pill, and a primitive named badge, pill, chip or tag-capsule; scripts/check-style-literals.mjs refuses a pill radius and those class names in the stylesheets.
//   themes:        presets. A preset gives every token a value: `shared` (both schemes), `light` and `dark` (every colour token is in both). A value of the form "{token}" refers to another token of the same preset. `variants` lists named choices per dimension (the dimension's `defaults` value is the base); a variant gives only the tokens it changes. `from` derives a preset from another and overrides some tokens. `acceptedShortfalls` names a pair that is known to fall short, with a floor the ratio may not drop under and the reason.
{
  "version": 1,
  "defaultTheme": "fieldnotes",
  "tokens": [
    {"id":"surface","group":"Surfaces","type":"colour"},
    {"id":"surface-sunk","group":"Surfaces","type":"colour"},
    {"id":"surface-raised","group":"Surfaces","type":"colour"},
    {"id":"surface-overlay","group":"Surfaces","type":"colour"},
    {"id":"text","group":"Text","type":"colour"},
    {"id":"text-muted","group":"Text","type":"colour"},
